    {
      "feature_id": "chrome-5163880346812416",
      "source_feature_id": 5163880346812416,
      "title": "Chrome 내 Gemini",
      "source_url": "https://chromestatus.com/feature/5163880346812416",
      "kind": "policy_or_feature_reference",
      "summary": "기존 공식 Enterprise 항목 재관찰: Chrome 내 Gemini",
      "source_updated_at": "2026-10-22 20:31:15.042457",
      "announced_at": null,
      "effective_at": null,
      "enterprise_stages": [
        {
          "stage_type": 1061,
          "rollout_milestone": 151,
          "rollout_platforms": [
            "3",
            "6",
            "7"
          ],
          "rollout_stage_plan": 2,
          "rollout_details": "- Gemini in Chrome became available to users in the United Kingdom and 14 additional countries and territories.\n- File upload support: Users may upload files in Gemini in Chrome, enabling them to ask questions about files, such as comparing them with the content of their open tabs. In Chrome 151, this feature rolls out to consumers only, but Admins can set the [RestrictSigninToPattern](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/restrict-signin-to-pattern/) policy to restrict sign-ins from personal Gmail accounts, or use the [LocalUserFilesAllowed](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#LocalUserFilesAllowed) policy. In Chrome 152, Admins can use the GeminiChromeFileUploadSettings policy to control this feature directly.\n- File generation support: Users can generate files like Google Docs, Sheets, PDFs, and more directly from Gemini in Chrome. \n- Gemini in Chrome improved scam blocking: Safe Browsing protections have been expanded to provide an even safer experience during Gemini in Chrome interactions. By triggering real-time Safe Browsing verdicts for active pages, this update increases coverage to protect against newly created malicious sites and keep AI-assisted browsing secure. This update introduces no new enterprise policies. Existing enterprise policies governing Safe Browsing protections (such as [SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#SafeBrowsingProtectionLevel)) and generative AI features (such as [GenAiDefaultSettings](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#GenAiDefaultSettings)) continue to govern user access and warning behaviors across managed devices. For more information, see [Google Safe Browsing](https://safebrowsing.google.com/) and [Gemini in Chrome](https://support.google.com/chrome/a/answer/16291696).\n"
        },
        {
          "stage_type": 1061,
          "rollout_milestone": 154,
          "rollout_platforms": [
            "2",
            "3",
            "6",
            "7"
          ],
          "rollout_stage_plan": 2,
          "rollout_details": "- Try it on: Users can now virtually try on clothes, right in context of their favorite brands with shopping insights in Gemini in Chrome. This feature is not yet available with all retailers and only available for US-en users. Admins can control this feature using a new enterprise policy is TryOnYouSettings.\n- Gemini Live in Chrome for iOS: Enables real-time, voice-driven conversations in Chrome iOS to discuss active page content with Gemini while browsing.\n"
        },
        {
          "stage_type": 1061,
          "rollout_milestone": 156,
          "rollout_platforms": [
            "1",
            "3",
            "6",
            "7"
          ],
          "rollout_stage_plan": 0,
          "rollout_details": "- On Chrome on Android, users can background an auto browse task and see the status update through a live notification instead of a Picture in Picture.\n- On desktop, Gemini in Chrome now supports creating Quizzes, enabling the user to transform any web page, PDF, slide deck, Youtube video, and more into an interactive study session. Initially available to limited countries and languages.\n"
        },
        {
          "stage_type": 1061,
          "rollout_milestone": 150,
          "rollout_platforms": [
            "3",
            "6",
            "7"
          ],
          "rollout_stage_plan": 0,
          "rollout_details": "- Gemini Spark can use Chrome auto browse to complete tasks that need web actuation. Enterprise policy is [GeminiSparkSettings](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#GeminiSparkSettings).\n- Chrome will also now suggest Gemini in Chrome features at relevant moments. Enterprise policy is [ChromeSuggestionsSettings](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#ChromeSuggestionsSettings)."
        },
        {
          "stage_type": 1061,
          "rollout_milestone": 157,
          "rollout_platforms": [
            "1",
            "2",
            "3",
            "5",
            "6",
            "7"
          ],
          "rollout_stage_plan": 2,
          "rollout_details": "* The **AutofillPredictionSettings** policy is superseded by [AutofillGenAiSettings](https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#AutofillGenAiSettings) policy (available starting in Chrome 156).\n"
        }
      ],
      "summary_sha256": "c443d1785839dd0bc19c9533b2c3452fb2e7e28a6b39a9960d00212833c901b5",
